ALREADY APPLIED ON THIS BRANCH (feature/connect-meeting-mode) — do not apply.

.env.example is a shared root file; this patch is the record of the lane
crossing, and the change itself is in the branch (with a Windows-safe key
command added beyond what this hunk shows — the branch copy is the truth).
`git apply` would fail on already-applied context. Kept as documentation.
git apply tolerates this leading text; it reads from the first ---/+++ pair.

--- a/.env.example
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -40,3 +40,21 @@
 SENTRY_DSN=
 RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
 RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
+
+# --- Connect: private (encrypted) meetings --------------------------------
+# The secret the per-meeting media key is derived from. Unset means Private
+# meetings are switched OFF on this server; Recorded meetings are unaffected.
+# Must be long and random — anything under 32 characters is IGNORED, because
+# a weak key here looks like encryption without being it.
+#
+#   openssl rand -base64 48
+#
+# ROTATING THIS HAS A CONSEQUENCE, AND IT IS NOT A SURPRISE:
+# every meeting's key is derived from it, so anyone who JOINS OR REJOINS a
+# private meeting after a rotation derives the new key and will see and hear
+# nothing from the people already in the room. It clears when that meeting
+# ends. Rotate BETWEEN meetings, never during one.
+#
+# Distinct from JWT_SIGNING_KEY on purpose: one secret per purpose, so
+# rotating or leaking one does not touch the other.
+CONNECT_ROOM_KEY_SECRET=
